ugrep installs command-line tools, not a linkable library:

    <installed-prefix>/tools/ugrep/ugrep[.exe]
    <installed-prefix>/tools/ugrep/ugrep-indexer[.exe]

PCRE2 is required for -P. This port builds without optional compression libraries,
Boost.Regex, ug aliases, or shell wrappers. Native Linux/macOS and Windows
x86/x64 builds are admitted; cross compilation and UWP are not supported.
The qigao-x64-windows-llvm-mingw-static triplet builds the LLVM-MinGW tool
with static PCRE2 and C++ runtime linkage. Windows system DLLs remain required.

For build-time use, declare { "name": "ugrep", "host": true } in your manifest
and locate the executable under the host installed prefix.

For runtime use, select a package for the actual runtime platform. A build-host
tool is not a runtime-target executable when cross compiling.
